{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"artifacts":[{"contents":{"text":"<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\" version=\"1.0\" datamodel=\"ecmascript\" initial=\"a\">\n  <datamodel><data id=\"a1\"/><data id=\"b1\"/></datamodel>\n  <state id=\"a\"><onentry><send event=\"t\" namelist=\"a1,b1\"/></onentry><transition event=\"t\" target=\"f\"/></state><final id=\"f\"/>\n</scxml>\n"},"location":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml039-namelist-commas.scxml"},"mimeType":"application/scxml+xml"}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits","properties":{"diagnosticCounts":{"errors":0,"notes":0,"total":1,"warnings":1},"producer":{"kind":"validator"}},"results":[{"fixes":[{"artifactChanges":[{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml039-namelist-commas.scxml"},"replacements":[{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":5,"byteOffset":204,"endColumn":57,"endLine":3,"startColumn":52,"startLine":3},"insertedContent":{"text":"a1 b1"}}]}],"description":{"text":"separate the names with spaces"},"properties":{"applicability":"machine-applicable"}}],"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml039-namelist-commas.scxml"},"region":{"endColumn":57,"endLine":3,"startColumn":52,"startLine":3}}}],"message":{"markdown":"`namelist` separates names with spaces, not commas: `a1,b1` is not one location\n\n**Note:** `namelist` is a space-separated list of data-model locations; a comma makes the list one name that is not a valid location\n\n**Help:** separate the names with spaces: `a1 b1`\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §6.2 <send>\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model","text":"`namelist` separates names with spaces, not commas: `a1,b1` is not one location"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":209,"start":204},"category":"lint"},"ruleId":"SCXML039"}],"tool":{"driver":{"informationUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/","name":"scxml-validator","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"`location`, `idlocation`, `namelist` items, and `<foreach item/index>` must name an assignable place; SCXML 1.0 defines the run-time outcome of one that does not, so the document compiles: §5.9.2 \"If a location expression cannot be evaluated to yield a valid location, the SCXML processor MUST place the error 'error.execution' in the internal event queue\", and §4.6 \"if 'item' does not specify a legal variable name, the SCXML processor MUST terminate execution of the <foreach> element and the block that contains it, and place the error error.execution on the internal event queue\". In ECMAScript an assignable place is a variable or a property access such as `data.field` or `data[0]`; in XPath it is an expression that selects existing nodes, such as `$data` or `$data/field` (`a.b` is one variable name containing a dot, and `a[0]` is a predicate)"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: ECMAScript: use a variable name or a member expression such as `data.field`; XPath: use a `$`-rooted path to a declared variable such as `$data/field`.\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §5.9.2 Location Expressions\n\nRun `scxml-cli --explain SCXML039` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#LocationExpressions","id":"SCXML039","name":"SCXML039","properties":{"category":"semantic"},"shortDescription":{"text":"a location is not assignable in the selected data model"}}],"semanticVersion":"0.2.0"}}}],"version":"2.1.0"}